Step 1 - Understand the problem
Write a debounce function in JavaScript.

Step 2 - Plan the solution
1. Keep a timer variable in a closure.
2. On every call clear the previous timer.
3. Start a new timer that runs the function after the delay.

Step 3 - Write the code
function debounce(fn, delay) {
  let timer;
  return function (...args) {
    clearTimeout(timer);
    timer = setTimeout(() => fn.apply(this, args), delay);
  };
}

Step 4 - Test it and check edge cases
Call it 5 times quickly. The original function should run only once, after the delay.

Note: Used for search boxes and window resize handlers.

