Step 1 - Understand the problem
Write a C function to check if a number is prime.

Step 2 - Plan the solution
1. Return false for numbers below 2.
2. Test divisors from 2 while i * i <= n.
3. If any divisor divides n evenly return false, otherwise return true.

Step 3 - Write the code
#include <stdbool.h>

bool is_prime(int n) {
    if (n < 2) return false;
    for (int i = 2; i * i <= n; i++) {
        if (n % i == 0) return false;
    }
    return true;
}

Step 4 - Test it and check edge cases
is_prime(2) -> true, is_prime(1) -> false, is_prime(97) -> true

Note: Time O(sqrt n). Needs #include <stdbool.h>.

