Step 1 - Understand the problem
Write a C function to reverse a string in place.

Step 2 - Plan the solution
1. Use two indexes: i at the start and j at the last character.
2. Swap s[i] and s[j], then move i forward and j backward.
3. Stop when i >= j.

Step 3 - Write the code
#include <string.h>

void reverse_string(char *s) {
    int i = 0, j = (int)strlen(s) - 1;
    while (i < j) {
        char tmp = s[i];
        s[i] = s[j];
        s[j] = tmp;
        i++;
        j--;
    }
}

Step 4 - Test it and check edge cases
Works on a modifiable array like char s[] = "hello". It crashes on a string literal like char *s = "hello".

Note: Time O(n), space O(1).

